{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"O95786","uniProtkbId":"RIGI_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Antiviral innate immune response receptor RIG-I"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"19211564"}],"value":"ATP-dependent RNA helicase DDX58"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19211564"}],"value":"3.6.4.13"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"DEAD box protein 58"}},{"fullName":{"value":"RIG-I-like receptor 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"RLR-1"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:19102"}],"value":"RNA sensor RIG-I"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Retinoic acid-inducible gene 1 protein"},"shortNames":[{"value":"RIG-1"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Retinoic acid-inducible gene I protein"},"shortNames":[{"value":"RIG-I"}]}]},"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15208624"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15708988"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16125763"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16127453"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16153868"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17190814"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18636086"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19122199"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19211564"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19576794"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19609254"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19631370"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21742966"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24366338"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28469175"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29117565"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"31006531"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"34935440"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35263596"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"36793726"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"Reference","id":"Ref.74"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"21616437"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"21884169"}],"value":"Innate immune receptor that senses cytoplasmic viral nucleic acids and activates a downstream signaling cascade leading to the production of type I interferons and pro-inflammatory cytokines (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988, PubMed:16125763, PubMed:16127453, PubMed:16153868, PubMed:17190814, PubMed:18636086, PubMed:19122199, PubMed:19211564, PubMed:24366338, PubMed:28469175, PubMed:29117565, PubMed:31006531, PubMed:34935440, PubMed:35263596, PubMed:36793726). Forms a ribonucleoprotein complex with viral RNAs on which it homooligomerizes to form filaments (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988). The homooligomerization allows the recruitment of RNF135 an E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that activates and amplifies the RIG-I-mediated antiviral signaling in an RNA length-dependent manner through ubiquitination-dependent and -independent mechanisms (PubMed:28469175, PubMed:31006531). Upon activation, associates with mitochondria antiviral signaling protein (MAVS/IPS1) that activates the IKK-related kinases TBK1 and IKBKE which in turn phosphorylate the interferon regulatory factors IRF3 and IRF7, activating transcription of antiviral immunological genes including the IFN-alpha and IFN-beta interferons (PubMed:28469175, PubMed:31006531). Ligands include 5'-triphosphorylated ssRNAs and dsRNAs but also short dsRNAs (<1 kb in length) (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988, PubMed:19576794, PubMed:19609254, PubMed:21742966). In addition to the 5'-triphosphate moiety, blunt-end base pairing at the 5'-end of the RNA is very essential (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988, PubMed:19576794, PubMed:19609254, PubMed:21742966). Overhangs at the non-triphosphorylated end of the dsRNA RNA have no major impact on its activity (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988, PubMed:19576794, PubMed:19609254, PubMed:21742966). A 3'overhang at the 5'triphosphate end decreases and any 5'overhang at the 5' triphosphate end abolishes its activity (PubMed:15208624, PubMed:15708988, PubMed:19576794, PubMed:19609254, PubMed:21742966). Detects both positive and negative strand RNA viruses including members of the families Paramyxoviridae: Human respiratory syncytial virus and measles virus (MeV), Rhabdoviridae: vesicular stomatitis virus (VSV), Orthomyxoviridae: influenza A and B virus, Flaviviridae: Japanese encephalitis virus (JEV), hepatitis C virus (HCV), dengue virus (DENV) and west Nile virus (WNV) (PubMed:21616437, PubMed:21884169). It also detects rotaviruses and reoviruses (PubMed:21616437, PubMed:21884169). Detects and binds to SARS-CoV-2 RNAs which is inhibited by m6A RNA modifications (Ref.74). Also involved in antiviral signaling in response to viruses containing a dsDNA genome such as Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) (PubMed:19631370). Detects dsRNA produced from non-self dsDNA by RNA polymerase III, such as Epstein-Barr virus-encoded RNAs (EBERs). May play important roles in granulocyte production and differentiation, bacterial phagocytosis and in the regulation of cell migration"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"value":"Colocalized with TRIM25 at cytoplasmic perinuclear bodies. Associated with the actin cytoskeleton at membrane ruffles"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}},{"location":{"value":"Cell projection, ruffle membrane","id":"SL-0301"}},{"location":{"value":"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton","id":"SL-0090"}},{"location":{"value":"Cell junction, tight junction","id":"SL-0265"}}]}],"features":[{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":87,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"CARD 1"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":92,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":172,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"CARD 2"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":251,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":430,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helicase ATP-binding","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU00541"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":610,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":776,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helicase C-terminal","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU00542"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":794,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":925,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"RLR CTR","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU01125"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":218,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":925,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Interaction with ZC3HAV1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21102435"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":735,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":925,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mediates interaction with RNF135","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23950712"}]},{"type":"Motif","location":{"start":{"value":372,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":375,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"DECH box"},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":264,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":271,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","featureCrossReferences":[{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"ligand":{"name":"ATP","id":"ChEBI:CHEBI:30616"}},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":810,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":810,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"desc